{"name":"Boy Blue","hex":"#8cacd6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bodo (Central Africa)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A young man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boy Blue (Electric Light Orchestra song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Boy Blue\" is a song written by Jeff Lynne and performed by the Electric Light Orchestra (ELO) which first appeared as the third track from their 1974 album Eldorado."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Boy_Blue_single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy_Blue_(Electric_Light_Orchestra_song)"},{"title":"Boy Blue (Fables)","blocks":[{"text":"Boy Blue is a major character in the Vertigo comic book series Fables. He is based on the nursery rhyme character Little Boy Blue. At the beginning of the series, he is portrayed as an efficient but meek office clerk helping Snow White run Fabletown, but he has a colorful and violent history that is gradually revealed as the series goes on."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Bluefables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy_Blue_(Fables)"},{"title":"Boy","blocks":[{"text":"A boy is a young male human. The term is commonly used for a child or an adolescent. When a male human reaches adulthood, they are usually described as a man."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg/330px-Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AViews_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Napoli%2C_scugnizzi.jpg/500px-Napoli%2C_scugnizzi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x